#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147140 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b508e1a-00f5-58d1-b399-344884761c8e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Multiplication of Fractions by Whole Numbers as Multiplication and Division"}] :question/id #uuid "a3ef9728-84fb-50d0-a50b-774386ca7c9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12570" :question/problem "What is missing from the statement below?\n\n$$\n10 \\times \\dfrac{2}{5} = \\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}} \\div \\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}} \\times 2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as:\n\n$$\n10 \\times 2\\div 5\n$$\n\nWe can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $\\times 2$ and the $\\div 5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{10} \\div \\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{5} \\times 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is $10 \\div 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147141 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147458 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdcb850d-14d5-56e9-81d8-9af497460503" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Multiplication and Division as Multiplication of Fractions by Whole Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "b8af91a0-f5c0-545e-b188-b62cde696bb8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12571" :question/problem "What fraction is missing from the statement below?\n\n![](images/fb/fb748fd8124576b52ee9af881b5559ac005e2a50615ba9b6604269fbce002d38.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $\\div 5$ and the $\\times 20\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n7 \\times 20 \\div 5\n$$\n\nWe can now interpret the division as a fraction:\n\n$$\n7\\times \\dfrac{20}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing fraction is $\\dfrac{20}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147142 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147459 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfdc6b8f-e329-57b4-9ae9-e2f2c92105be" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Multiplier and the Numerator of a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "812e5cc8-ff6f-5e67-84bf-f012dec63466" :question/math-academy-id "e-12572" :question/problem "What fraction is missing from the statement below?\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{4}\\times 8= 5 \\times \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{\\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as:\n\n$$\n5\\div 4\\times 8\n$$\n\nWe can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $\\div 4$ and the $\\times 8{:}$\n\n$$\n5\\times 8\\div 4\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the $8\\div 4$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n5\\times \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{8}}{\\bbox[2pt, border:1pt solid black]{4}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147143 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147460 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5726ea5c-ba64-51c2-b5ac-0915853fd080" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating an Expression by Interpreting a Fraction as Division"}] :question/id #uuid "dfa40a5c-e8ed-55c0-83e7-bd701eae0da5" :question/math-academy-id "e-12573" :question/problem "Evaluate $21 \\times \\dfrac{7}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as:\n\n$$\n21\\times 7\\div 3\n$$\n\nWe can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $\\times 7$ and the $\\div 3{:}$\n\n$$\n21 \\div 3\\times 7\n$$\n\nExpressing the division as a fraction, we arrive at:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{21}{3}\\times 7\n$$\n\nWe now solve:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\dfrac{21}{3}}_{7}\\times 7 = 7\\times 7 = 49.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b508e1a-00f5-58d1-b399-344884761c8e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Multiplication of Fractions by Whole Numbers as Multiplication and Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "127e41ad-8e42-596a-a6f3-5c349e